  "description": "WIYGAP crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C80 H98 Dy6 N4 O36 Zn4,4(C1 H4 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Zn1 (Zn) has 4 O neighbors; Zn2 (Zn) has 5 O neighbors; Dy1A (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy2A (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy3A (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Zn1A (Zn) has 4 O neighbors; Zn2A (Zn) has 5 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 23 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.310-4.001 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 88.69-127.01°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Dy6Zn4O2(L)2(HL)2(OAc)8(CH3O)4(H2O)2]·4MeOH. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 8 OAc (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
